      "id": "claim_1ae40d9690df47ea9fcac28c0dc3bb78",
      "statement": "The kernel security boundary is a nine-stage pipeline (Admission, Claimed execution, Trust ceiling, Authorization, Approval, Reservation, Policy planning, Membrane, Mediated execution) that every privileged effect must pass through. Each stage is owned by a separate crate with its own fail-closed invariant.",
